  "post_hoc": "[MEASURE] POST-HOC (2026-10-29): replay of the released E8 comparator arm and rescoring of every certified row against the closed-form site-population R_M; the frozen CSV is unchanged and no certified quantity descends from this file. The population scoring is a second estimand for the same certificates, not a correction of the first.",
  "estimand": "rm_fresh is the released Section 3.9 metric: the certificate's influence-weighted R_M on one fresh 200-site pool, which carries that pool's sampling noise. rm_population is the parameter the certificate names, E[g a e] / E[g a] over the site population, in closed form: site size is drawn independently of the site effect, so the influence weights cancel and R_M = E_u[P_u(ans & err)] / E_u[P_u(ans)], linear in the site prevalence, evaluated at pibar = E[sigmoid(logit 0.095 + 0.5 Z)] with the head's logit Gaussian within each class. An exceedance is R_M > alpha under either scoring.",
  "headline": "a=0.05 pooled over 6 site counts: Student-t 61/1200 on the fresh pool -> 46/1200 against the population R_M (CI [0.028199, 0.050802]); site bootstrap 59 -> 45 (CI [0.027482, 0.049858]); WSR, MP-EB and Hoeffding 0 under both; all 6056 certified rows replayed (tau exact, rm_fresh 6 dp)",
  "pibar": 0.10365668,
  "closed_form": "R_M = [pibar Phi((-l-m1)/s) + (1-pibar) Phi((m0-l)/s)] / [pibar (Phi((m1-l)/s) + Phi((-l-m1)/s)) + (1-pibar) (Phi((m0-l)/s) + Phi((-l-m0)/s))], l = logit(tau), w = coef/sd, b = intercept - w.mu_head, m_y = b + w.mu_y, s = ||w||",
